# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Ablation caches ARE TRACKED as of 2026-09-05. They were ignored as
# "regenerable, and large" — the first is true and the second was not: all four
# together are 141 KB, against roughly six hours of simulation to rebuild them.
# Tracking them lets a clone reproduce or extend the four tables without that
# run. The cost is that a stale cache can now arrive with a checkout, so
# ABLATION_CACHES.md records a source fingerprint per deck; check it before
# resuming one. See cache_manifest.py.

# Spreadsheet lock/temp files
~$*.xlsx
.~lock.*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Ablation stderr progress logs — noise, the .txt tables are the artefact
ablation_*.log

# Regeneration scratch — the finished .txt tables ARE tracked
ablation_*.txt.new
regen.log

# A void table kept only long enough to diff against; not an artefact.
ablation_*_VOID_*.txt
